REQUEST:
Pick whichever fitting one costs the least, please. My roommate Dana asked me to pick up a clock for our hallway, and she's got feelings about what goes on that wall. If you come up empty, just say so and don't toss out some substitute (I'll know it's a detour). (I figured a clock's a clock, but I'll be fair, she's lived here longer.) That wall is the first thing folks see coming in, like the overlook at the top of a trail, so whatever I pick sets the tone. Only count what you've got on hand in the store, not what's just listed on some website somewhere (I've been burned by that before). It's a clock I'm after, and the shape's got to be square (I'll check it myself, don't worry, I ain't taking anybody's word on faith). Nothing over 725 cts, y'all (student loans ain't gonna pay themselves, and every penny counts for me, like every step on a steep climb). Total, you can send me 3 messages and no more than that. Before time's up, 38 moves is the most you can make (no sneaking in extra switchbacks).

REQUIREMENTS IN FORCE:
- item: clock, quantity 1; requirements: shape: square
- budget: at most 725 cents in total
- pick: the cheapest listing that fits (lowest price)
- in stock only
- rule from the request: Count only items stocked in the store, not website listings.
- rule from the request: Do not suggest substitutes when nothing fits.
- rule from the request: Send no more than 3 messages.
- rule from the request: Use no more than 38 steps.
- if nothing fits: end without naming or suggesting any listing
- listing attributes come from datasheet_for_item; a listing's page (what a chain of pages or a page check means) is shown by view_listing

